<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26026" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lātrātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				barker</i> (perh. not ante-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <b>poet.</b> for <i>a dog</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Molossi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					12, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Anubis (who is represented with the head of a
					dog),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 698</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9, 690</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a bawler,
			brawler</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a viro bono in rabulam latratoremque converti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 12, 9, 12</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
